From 44219f6d0833dd705e5d95f95c1c207cf9b884cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilPatrick06 <187923600+EvilPatrick06@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:02:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A Claude subscription limit that reopens early lifts the
 login's model bench

An Anthropic 429 benches the OAuth login for the refused model until the
reset the response named, days out for a subscription's weekly window. The
window can reopen sooner (a reset given to the account, a plan change), and
only the OAuth usage endpoint says so. Codex has that check (#43747);
Anthropic had none, so a session pinned to its fallback stayed there until
the old reset time, and so did every new pick of the login.

The pool now asks the usage endpoint, throttled per token and model and
failing closed, when it lifts cooldowns for a model whose bench has longer
to run than the probe interval, and records a verified reopen as a reset so
the disk's older cooldown is not merged back over it. The restore path asks
for an Anthropic primary as it does for a Codex one.
